# tally 2.2.1 (#221, 221.R2), L §5.19: "A window belongs in an attribute (a giver's acquisition day), never in the
# observation's on". bank[g1]'s bought is window(2019-01-01, 2019-12-31): the row loads, the attribute reads as that
# window (d), year_of and a comparison decide on it (y, e). tally 2.2 refused it at load (LOAD-UNIT a value of the
# wrong type).
=== obsw.tally
model ow
  tally 2
  on 2026-08-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind gift: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
  attr bought: date
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  bank[g1] = (on: 2026-04-10, kind: gift, leg cash from world to konto amount 50.00 PLN, bought: window(2019-01-01, 2019-12-31)) "g1"
ask b: bal(konto, 2026-04-30)
ask d: bank[g1].bought
ask y: year_of(bank[g1].bought)
ask e: bank[g1].bought < 2020-01-01
=== expect
b: 50.00 PLN
  cut 2026-08-01
d: window(2019-01-01, 2019-12-31)
  cut 2026-08-01
e: true
  cut 2026-08-01
y: 2019
  cut 2026-08-01
